---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/use-cases/loyalty';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'use-cases/loyalty');
const desc = description(site, 'use-cases/loyalty');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "When should I invite a buyer?",
    "answer": "When program eligibility and benefits are clear; an order count alone does not establish the right timing."
  },
  {
    "question": "Who owns the points balance?",
    "answer": "The loyalty ledger. Email should use its current record and provide account access."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can a VIP exist outside loyalty?",
    "answer": "Yes. Keep behavioral segments separate from membership and explain the benefit rules."
  },
  {
    "question": "What if a queued balance becomes stale?",
    "answer": "Refresh or cancel it, or use a current account link without a potentially incorrect number."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <article class="container prose-shopify py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/use-cases">All use cases</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Loyalty email for Shopify: balances, rewards and recognition</h1>
    <p>Help members understand what they have earned and how to use it. Choose email tooling around the loyalty ledger, account access and program rules before choosing templates.</p>
    <section class="py-8">
      <h2>Make the loyalty ledger authoritative</h2>
      <p>Write down which system owns membership, available points, pending points, tier and expiry. Email should display that record rather than calculate a second balance. Include the record timestamp and a link to the current account balance when synchronization can lag. A refunded order, redeemed reward or merged account can make yesterday’s email incorrect.</p>
      <p>Decide which changes deserve a message: enrollment confirmation, reward availability, tier change and an approaching expiry under your actual terms. A purchase event is not itself proof that points are available. Pending points should be described as pending, and reversals should explain the underlying adjustment without promising an unavailable reward.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="py-8">
      <h2>Enrollment is a program decision</h2>
      <p>Offer membership when the benefits are relevant and the terms can be explained. There is no universal second-order enrollment rule. Distinguish an invitation from confirmed enrollment; purchase, newsletter subscription and membership are separate states. Define eligibility for wholesale customers rather than assuming consumer rules apply.</p>
      <p>A loyalty tier and a behavioral VIP segment can overlap without being identical. Keep the tier supplied by the program separate from any spending-based segment used for launch access. State which benefit comes from which qualification so a segment update does not silently promise a tier upgrade.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="py-8">
      <h2>Design redemption and expiry messages</h2>
      <p>Show the actual reward, eligible products, restrictions, expiry date and timezone, and a usable account path. Distinguish points expiry from an already-issued reward coupon expiring. Avoid converting a points balance into a cash value unless the program’s conversion and redemption terms support it.</p>
      <p>Marsello documents that customers sharing an email address share a points balance and available rewards. This is a concrete identity risk to examine during account cleanup. Its documentation does not establish that every external email platform receives every balance or expiry field. Ask for a demonstration of your own account and integration path.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="py-8">
      <h2>A proposed reconciliation exercise</h2>
      <p>For an outdoor retailer, create internal test accounts representing an in-store purchase, an online purchase, a return and an existing redeemed reward. Compare the ledger, queued message and account page. Replay a tier event and confirm it does not generate a second celebration. This is a proposed acceptance exercise, not a merchant result.</p>
      <p>Then change the expiry or redeem while a reminder is queued. Decide whether the message is cancelled, refreshed or replaced by a link-only reminder. If current balance cannot be trusted, omit the stale number. Assign support a way to inspect the source transaction and correct discrepancies.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="py-8">
      <h2>Choose a stack and measure the program</h2>
      <p>A single loyalty-and-email system reduces handoffs; separate tools may offer more editorial control but add identity mapping, sync monitoring and ownership work. Include Sequenzy, Marsello or an existing email provider only as candidates that must demonstrate your required events, fields and account links. Compare costs using actual membership and message volumes, not an unsupported ranking.</p>
      <p>Track delivered invitations, confirmed enrollments, reward use, balance-related support and repeat purchases by enrollment cohort. Members may already be stronger repeat buyers, so a cohort difference is not proof that the email caused it. Test optional promotional reminders separately from essential account communication, and record exclusions and measurement windows before comparing outcomes.</p>
    </section>
    <p>Primary reference checked November 25, 2026: <a class="link" href="https://help.marsello.com/loyalty-rewards-common-questions-marsello-help-center">Marsello reward and shared-account documentation</a>. Workflow recommendations and proposed checks above are editorial guidance, not claims of completed testing.</p>
    <p>Continue with <a class="link" href="/use-cases/vip-segments">vip segments</a>, <a class="link" href="/use-cases/replenishment">replenishment</a>. Browse the <a class="link" href="/apps">tool catalog</a> for candidates; confirm current capabilities and costs for the required integration.</p>
  </article>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Loyalty FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
